{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1490036488,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4Nzg2NDAyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1388#issuecomment-287864028"},"message":"Looks like this is on an NFS mount? I cannot find it now, but we had such observation before -- delay of several minutes. Not related to `add` AFAIK, but looked like a more general NFS + git + annex issue.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1490036695,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4Nzg2NDk4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1388#issuecomment-287864983"},"message":"Here #721","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1490042384,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4Nzg5MDU0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1388#issuecomment-287890547"},"message":"nope -- this one straight on btrfs mount\n```shell\n$\u003e df /mnt/datasets/datalad/crawl/openfmri \nFilesystem       1K-blocks        Used   Available Use% Mounted on\n/dev/md10      46883131392 31625666308 15255454108  68% /mnt/datasets\n\n$\u003e mount | grep mnt/datasets\n/dev/md10 on /mnt/datasets type btrfs (rw,noatime,compress=lzo,space_cache,subvolid=1478,subvol=/datasets)\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1490186545,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4ODM4NjY1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1388#issuecomment-288386657"},"message":"I don't know why you don't get debug output - I do.\nIt doesn't take much time for me, but it probably depends on the size of the subdataset, which is admittedly a bad and unnecessary thing.\n`datalad add` (at least in master) uses `git add` and a subsequent call to `git annex add`. Additionally a dry run of `git add .`. I think that kind of analyzing what exactly to add leads to a lot of overhead in that case.\n\nI think we should have a more compound `Repo.add_submodule` to be called by `datalad add`. This one should include the `git submodule add` as well as the committing of the subdataset and `.gitmodules`. And it should account for direct mode / v6.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1490187135,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4ODM4ODgxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1388#issuecomment-288388816"},"message":"Before caring for that, please note, that there is in issue with committing submodules in direct mode, as shown in PR #1277 . So that's the kind of \"compound operations\" I was talking about.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1490192912,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4ODQxNTk1Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1388#issuecomment-288415953"},"message":"@bpoldrack there is a **long** period of silence in debug messages --- that is where all that recursive traversal is happening fishing out the subdatasets.  Yes -- this symptom is for large datasets.  Try e.g. `datalad install /-r //` to your laptop and play within it then ;)  But my point in #1407 that traversal is often just too aggressive in many cases for no good reason","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1490263962,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTAxMjEwNzkyNw=="},"status":2}]}